Well, so it depends. So it depends. If I have metastasis to the spine, I might not really have any pain whatsoever until there is a degree of bone loss that could cause a fracture.

00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:59,240
So when I have a fracture from caused from bone loss because of metastasis to the bone that's called a pathological fracture. So it's not a fracture because I fell down the stairs. It's a fracture because it broke because of lack of bone density because of a lytic lesion in the case of metastasis.

00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:14,240
So a person may not have any bone pain with metastasis to the bone. A person may have bone pain. If they do have bone pain, it would feel like a deep ache, a deep ache.

00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:27,240
Now, if it was a metastasis to the spine and now you have pain because that vertebral body let's say fractured, then that fracture causes a decrease in height of the vertebral body.

